Prints the node relay's state: the compiled tools.mcp_access table and
the vservers it approves, remote forwarding (an idempotent registration
against the org server unless --no-remote), which client configs are
VERIFIED projected, the relay point's effective state and hash, the
hash-chained decision record, and the coverage matrix.

With [mcp_relay].enabled = false it reports the relay disabled and makes
no org-server call; it still lists client configs the journal shows as
wrapped (switched off without `observer mcp unwrap`).

Usage:
  observer mcp status [flags]

Flags:
      --config string   path to config.toml (default ~/.observer/config.toml)
  -h, --help            help for status
      --json            print JSON
      --no-matrix       omit the coverage matrix
      --no-remote       do not probe remote forwarding (no org-server registration call)
